    "report": "The archive feature is finished and committed as `5a6e846` on `main`, the branch you asked for. Nothing is pushed. `main` is also the default branch, so this commit lands directly on it. Say if you wanted a feature branch instead.\n\n**What the previous developer left:** the aggregate's archive rule, its persistence, and a domain spec. That work was sound. What was missing was the command wiring, the route, the list filter, and the tests.\n\n**What I added:**\n- **Route and command:** `POST /conversations/:id/archive`, answered with `acceptCommand` like `read`. The handler is registered in the Messaging module.\n- **List:** `GET /conversations/mine` leaves out conversations the caller archived at their last message. A new message by anyone brings them back. The unread total still counts archived conversations, because it reads the same query without the filter.\n- **SQL:** `findSummaries` returns an `archived` flag, computed against the conversation's current last message. The read model and port docs are updated to match.\n- **Tests:** eight new e2e cases in `conversations.routes.e2e.spec.ts`. They cover the list, re-archiving, return on a new message, the other readers, a viewer, a stranger, a missing id, and no sign-in.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Typecheck, lint, and prettier pass.\n- Unit tests: 156 suites, 1052 tests pass.\n- E2E: 114 suites, 610 tests pass. I ran these with a larger heap because the single full `yarn test` run exhausted Node's default heap.\n\n**Choices I made where the request was open:**\n- The archive is tied to the conversation's last message, including hidden messages. This matches the domain's existing \"last message\" rule.\n- A refusal (stranger, missing id) shows as an `ERROR` operation, as `read` does. Only the not-signed-in case gets an immediate 401.\n- Archiving again changes nothing observable. It still writes the conversation row, as `read` does, which bumps its stored version.\n\n**Not done:**\n- I did not add the archive command to `conventions/storms/conversations.yaml`. Conventions are protected in feature mode, so that needs your go-ahead.\n- I did not start a server, so port 4471 was not used.",
